module gunbc.ambiguity_ban_admission

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import std.disposition { Disposition, Terminal }
import std.types { String }
import v2.std.collection { List }

data ambiguity_ban_receipt_disposition: Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "Single authority for the SEED-GROWTH RECEIPT owed by the ambiguity-ranking ban in the bare-reference closure resolver. It declares WHICH hand-authored Rust declarations that change adds to the seed, why they exist, and what retires them. It does NOT admit them: the realization disposition is an operator judgment and fails closed in its absence, because a receipt that also granted its own admission would be the self-authorized dissolution failure DESIGN names. Terminal because the RECEIPT is permanent -- it outlives the code it describes, recording what was owed and on what trigger it was discharged."
}

// WHY A NEW DISPOSITION IS REQUIRED RATHER THAN COVERAGE BY THE EXISTING ONE.
//
// gunbc.bare_reference_scanner_admission carries an operator disposition (ScaffoldAdmitted,
// 2026-08-24, gunbc#9102) whose boundary block is explicit about what it does NOT cover:
//
//   "NOT ADMITTED, each requiring a NEW disposition: additional source-text recognizers; new
//    callers of the scanner; public-surface growth; the whole-pool fallback; nearest-ancestor
//    ambiguity selection; a general hand-written namespace parser."
//
// This change lands two of those categories head-on, so reading it as covered would be reading
// an admission past the boundary its own author wrote:
//
//   - ADDITIONAL SOURCE-TEXT RECOGNIZER: explicit_import_member_names reads import blocks out of
//     raw source, including the multi-line form and the `A as B` alias binder.
//   - PUBLIC-SURFACE GROWTH: ClosureBareDisposition and closure_bare_disposition are `pub`.
//
// It also DELETES one of the categories rather than adding it -- nearest-ancestor ambiguity
// selection is exactly what this change removes from the closure resolver -- and that deletion is
// the reason the rest was written. That does not net against the additions: gunbc.seed_growth_admission
// states in its own note that netting deletions against additions is NOT IN SCOPE, and enforces it.

data ambiguity_ban_presumption_note: String = "THE PRESUMPTION AGAINST explicit_import_member_names STANDS AND IS NOT ARGUED AWAY. It re-derives from raw text a fact the parser already owns -- which local names an import binds -- and it sits in cli_run.rs beside a second line-scanning import reader, extract_import_paths. Two independent line parsers over the same grammar is the parallel-representation shape, and it did not stay theoretical: the first revision recognized only the single-line `import p { A }` form, so the resolver refused RankingDimension in dag/std/computation.dag, a file that DOES import it across a line break. The floor caught it. That is the drift argument landing as a real refusal, and it is evidence FOR the presumption, not against it.\n\nWHY IT EXISTS ANYWAY, stated as the cost of not having it: an import edge is the AUTHORITY for a name it names, and without subtracting those names the resolver consults the global census for a name the author already disambiguated -- so adding the disambiguating import would NOT silence the refusal the diagnostic itself prescribes as the remedy. A wall whose prescribed remedy does not work is worse than no wall.\n\nTHE TERMINAL CONSTRUCTION IS NOT THIS. It is occurrence provenance: the closure resolver consuming the canonical parsed import occurrence -- local_name, provider_module, exported_identity, occurrence_span -- rather than a BTreeSet<String> of spellings. A lexeme set cannot distinguish a resolved import from an unresolved path, a missing exported member, an alias from its provider, or two same-spelled occurrences in different scopes. Named by external review (review 58002) and accepted; not built here."

// WHAT IS NOT GROWTH AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED. Two existing items are MODIFIED, not added:
// bare_identifier_candidates (a caret-literal guard in its existing skip condition, and a bare
// assignment binder arm in its existing scan loop) and bare_reference_pull_paths_for_source (two
// new skip conditions and the ambiguity arm now projecting a named decision instead of ranking
// inline). Their disposition is ExistingSeedItemModified. Listing them here would inflate the
// addition census by two.

data ambiguity_ban_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run",
